# W307: text a detector must NOT find in the surface it reads.
#
# This file has an extension no walk in the tree matches — `sourceModules`, `typescriptFiles`,
# `testModules` and `textFiles` all filter on a list that does not include it — so text kept here
# is invisible to every scan while staying readable to a person. That is the whole mechanism, and
# `SELF_REFERENCE_RULE` in `scan-text.ts` is the sentence explaining why it beats the alternatives.
#
# Blocks are `=== name ===`; a block's text is everything up to the next header. `fixtureText`
# returns it with one trailing newline, `fixtureToken` returns it trimmed. Both directions are
# checked: a block nobody loads fails, and a `fixtureText("name")` for a block that is not here
# fails too — W258's citation rule, applied to fixtures.

